   "evidence": "The statement's left-hand side is `singularChainsCoinvariantsMap k (f \u226b q) (\u03c6 := \u03c8.comp \u03c6) (fun g x \u21a6 by rw [TopCat.comp_app, hf, hq]; rfl)`. `hf : \u2200 g x, f (g \u2022 x) = \u03c6 g \u2022 f x` and `hq` occur on the left only inside that proof term, so they are not determined by matching.",
   "file": "TauCeti/AlgebraicTopology/Singular/ModuleChains/EquivariantMap.lean",
   "fix": "Drop `@[simp]` and keep it as a named rewrite lemma. Add `@[reassoc]` for parity with the naturality squares in this PR.",
   "issue": "`@[simp]` on `singularChainsCoinvariantsMap_comp` cannot recover `hf`/`hq` from its left-hand side: they appear only inside a proof argument, which matches anything. So simp must prove the two equivariance hypotheses as side goals, which the default discharger generally cannot, and it only matches when the homomorphism is literally `\u03c8.comp \u03c6`. The lemma is effectively not a simp lemma.",
